The readme file that comes with this package gives a snotty reply
to those having trouble running it under Windows, saying that
there's a PIF and ICON file, so there should be no trouble.

Ho ho ho -- the joke is on us.  There's no PIF.  ;-)

I cannot get it to run under Windows, despite the fact that I have
*more* memory under Windows that I do under DOS (since I have a few
megs of virtual memory).  I am using Windows 3.1.  Does there have
to be a certain amount of conventional memory for it to run?  I
have 540K conventional memory under Windows and about 5M extended.

No matter what I do, under Windows I get this message:

DPMI: Not enough memory (0x00420000 bytes).

Is there some funky PIF setting that has to be set?  Does the
memory extender not get along with MS-DOS 6?  Does it not get
along with the Windows 3.1 DPMI server?

Has anyone gotten it running under Windows 3.1 and MS-DOS 6?

